To fix what didn't work for you, here are the three areas where web-based scanners usually fall short compared to the native CamScanner app:

Camera Quality & the "HD" Feature:

Capturing from a live <video> feed only grabs a 720p or 1080p video screenshot (often blurry for text).

True CamScanner quality needs full sensor resolution (12MP–48MP). We can switch the capture to use the native hardware camera API (ImageCapture / native camera intent) so the document is tack-sharp and legible.

Boundary Detection & Auto-Crop:

The lightweight radial edge tracker can easily get thrown off by wooden desk grain, shadows, or when the paper is tilted or off-center.

We can upgrade this to a full edge/contour detector (Canny edge + convex hull quad fitting) that reliably locks onto the 4 corners of the sheet and automatically slices away the desk background.

The Workflow:

In CamScanner, when you tap the shutter, it instantly snaps the 8 magnetic handles to the page edges and lets you confirm with one tap before dewarping flat into the Enhance screen.

Which part caused the biggest issue when you tested it?

Did the camera take a blurry/low-res photo?

Did the auto-detection miss the paper edges or crop the wrong area?

Or did the app feel sluggish / not open properly on your phone?

