I've completely overhauled the scanner engine to fix all three issues:

1. True HD Quality (ImageCapture API)
Why it was blurry before: Web browsers default <video> streams to 720p or 1080p video frames, which makes small text look pixelated.

The Fix: Captures now use the hardware-level ImageCapture.takePhoto() API, which triggers your phone’s camera sensor at its full native resolution (12MP–48MP) with autofocus before falling back to high-res video canvas.

Interactive HD Toggle: Tapping the HD button in the top bar now actively cycles between HD 1080p, Ultra HD 4K (Max Sensor), and Standard SD, dynamically updating your camera stream with on-screen resolution indicators (e.g. 1920x1080 or 3840x2160).

2. Auto-Boundary Detection & Automatic Desk Cropping
Real-Time Live Cyan Box: A multi-stage edge detector combines contrast quad-analysis and radial gradient rays to lock onto the 4 corners of your document (#00f0b5) with temporal smoothing.

Automatic Crop & Presentation: When you tap the shutter, the app automatically finds the document boundaries, cuts away the desk/table clutter, dewarps the page flat, and presents the clean document right in front of you on the Review screen.

Manual Crop Option: If you ever want to adjust corners manually, tapping Crop in the bottom bar opens the 4-corner crop tool with the 2.5x magnifying loupe.

3. Fixed the Black Screen in "Enhance" / "Magic Color"
Why it was black in your screenshot: A normalization bug was dividing pixel values by paper luminance twice, reducing brightness to near zero.

The Fix: Replaced with CamScanner's background luminance leveling: local paper brightness is normalized to pure white (#ffffff), desk shadows are removed, and text is sharpened without turning black.

